WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:02.560
What’s your favorite word?

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:04.160
Think about it for a moment.

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:05.840
Think real hard.

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:09.200
Write it down in the comments, post it for
everyone else to see.

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:10.960
How many letters does it have?

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:12.400
How many syllables?

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:13.520
Say it aloud.

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:14.720
How does it sound?

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:16.720
How does it feel on your tongue?

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:18.960
Really, really think about it.

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:23.600
Now, make sure you keep that word in mind,
it’s important, and we’ll come back to

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:24.400
it later.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:29.040
For now, it’s time to talk about SCP-3449.

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:31.600
Look, there’s really not anything special
about this one.

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:35.040
It wasn’t even important enough to be mentioned
with the other infohazards.

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:37.600
It’s no evil talking toaster, that’s for
sure.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:42.640
SCP-3449 appears to be just a standard spiral
notbook - notbook?

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:44.720
It’s supposed to be notebook, right?

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:48.720
Anyway, it’s a standard spiral notebook
with a dark blue cover.

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:53.840
It’s Safe-Class, and it’s stored in a
standred - ahem… a standard containment

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:55.600
locker in Site-19.

00:00:55.600 --> 00:01:00.040
There aren’t any other containment requires,
but testing is currently underway to determind

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:05.920
- I think that’s meant to be determine - long-term
containment requirements.

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:07.040
Ugh, this is a mess.

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:13.040
Anyway, this item and its anomalous power
is actually considered so inconsequential

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:17.680
that researchers have explored the possibility
of putting it on the anomalous items log,

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:21.280
a place where items too useless to warrant
a full file end uzp.

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:23.760
Jeez, how did you misspell “up” that badly?

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:26.880
It’s two letters, well it’s supposed to
be two letters.

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:30.240
How did you work a Z into that, they aren
’t even close to each other on the keyboard!

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:31.440
Man…

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:35.840
Anyway, the notebook contains mostly blank
pages.

00:01:35.840 --> 00:01:40.160
Some are torn, and only six contain actual
writing, but due to the formatting of the

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:44.800
writting, the text - consisting mainly of
diary entries - is almost unreadable.

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:50.560
This is due to syntactical errors, random
capitalization, and rampant impsmellings.

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:50.880
Great.

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:52.480
You misspelled misspellings.

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:54.720
How cute.

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:59.760
Apparently, all attempts to correct these
misspellings fail, or even lead to additional

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:00.960
misspellings.

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:07.840
This anomalous affect extends to anyone attempting
to right… yep, that was spelled r-i-g-h-t

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:15.600
- anyone attempting to write about SCP-3449,
including the script for this video apparently.

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:19.120
There are no further notable amonolous properties.

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:25.200
Tests are ongoing, those with any inquiries
about testing SCP-3449 should contact Lead

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:27.120
Researcher Niklo Gerdinel.

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:32.800
The notbok - which was misspelled even worse
that time… impressive - was first recovered

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:38.880
by MTF Epislon Six, also known as the Village
Idiots, after a series of infohazardous and

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:43.760
cognitohazardous phenomena were discovered
in the Pittsburgh Metrode Area.

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:49.600
The source seemed to be a storage unit filled
with anomalous items, and SCP-3449 was amogus

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:52.720
- I think that’s meant to be among - them.

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:57.920
The storage unit was registered to a man by
the name of Edward Selsburgh, currently designated

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:00.880
as Porpoise of Interest 4335.

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:02.400
Phew.

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:03.680
That’s the end of that.

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:08.480
Thanks for watching the video, folks, now
go check out- Oh, wait, there’s more.

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:15.360
Apparently that version of the file was an
older one, let’s check the next one and

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:17.840
see if that’s any more useful…Oh.

00:03:19.280 --> 00:03:20.160
Oh my.

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:23.280
It appears that the updates here are actually
quite extensive.

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:26.960
Okay, let’s give this another try.

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:35.760
SCP-3449 is a Euclid-Class SPC kept in the
humanid containment sells of Site-19.

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:41.360
Items affected by it are kept in standard
stroage lockers for Safe-Class anomalous objects

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:42.800
at the same site.

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:49.200
The primary reason for this shift is that
SCP-3449 has changed its object of designation:

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:55.840
It is no longer the spiral notebook, it is
now a 34-year-old Caucasian man known as Edward

00:03:55.840 --> 00:04:00.240
Selsburgh, formerly known as Person of Interest
4335.

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:05.280
He is believed to be the creator of the notbok,
as well as the other obects found inside the

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:07.520
storage looker in Pittsburgh.

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:14.000
Fundation personnel are now trying to locate
and contain any other objects created by Mr.

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:17.760
Selsburgh, though success has been lomited
on this front.

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:24.960
SCP-3449’s analogous abilities manifest
onto both Edward himself, and all the objects

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:26.320
created by him.

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:32.400
Wirting about him or any of these objects
will result in sytanictal errors, arbitrary

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:37.120
capitalizatoon, and rampart impsmellings.

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:41.280
Attempts to revise or correct the writing
will either fail to remove the errors, or

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:42.800
create new errors.

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:49.680
It appears that the anomalominous effects
of SCP-3449 proper are more severe than that

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:52.480
of the ones caused by his anomalous objects.

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:59.680
MTF Epsilon-6, also known as the Village Idyots,
apprehanded SCP-3449 in his apartment just

00:04:59.680 --> 00:05:01.600
outside of Prittsburgh.

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:07.040
He appeared to be in an advanced state of
disorontation and dehydration.

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:12.160
Records collected by the Mubile Task Force
found that Mr. Selburgh had not left his apratment

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:16.320
in over ten days, which would account for
his dire health conditions.

00:05:16.320 --> 00:05:22.160
Selsburgh did not communicate with mambas
of the Task Force, but did not resest arrest

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:24.080
and subsequent containment either.

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:29.280
Okay, okay, these spellings are rough, but
I’m going to try to power through.

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:32.400
We’re almost there.

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:39.680
The following is the full lug of items obtained
from SCP-3449’S storage locar that also

00:05:39.680 --> 00:05:42.240
exhibit his anomalous effects.

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:47.600
The Notebook - As already disgust, the pages
are either blank, torn, or illegible.

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:52.960
Selsburgh’s computer - Files saved on the
devise include spreadsheets detailing personal

00:05:52.960 --> 00:05:58.560
finances, ideas for products, and an unfinished
horror novel that is almost unraidable due

00:05:58.560 --> 00:06:00.800
to the pore quality of its writing.

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:06.080
Grocery List - Had only two written items:
“buter” was spelled with only one “t”,

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:10.000
and “medication” which was spelled “medicashun”.

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:14.640
A Planner - Last entry was dated two weeks
before containment, and believed to contain

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:19.280
reminders to perform various chores, however
a mixture of poor handwriting and word choice

00:06:19.280 --> 00:06:21.840
allows for other interpretations.

00:06:21.840 --> 00:06:24.480
And finally, Mr. Selsburgh’s cell phone.

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:28.720
Foundation researchers were able to collect
the call logs in hopes of further tracking

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:31.120
Selsburgh’s pre-containment activities.

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:36.160
The last three calls, which were all made
on the same day two weeks before continment,

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:39.760
dialed different numbers, only one of which
was in use.

00:06:39.760 --> 00:06:48.080
The Foundation made contact with the receiverer
of said call, who head no knowledge of SCP-3449,

00:06:48.080 --> 00:06:50.880
and claimed that they did not answer the call.

00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:58.160
Lead Researcher Niklo Gerdinel conduced the
first innerview with SCP-3449 shortly after

00:06:58.160 --> 00:06:59.120
his capture.

00:06:59.120 --> 00:07:04.800
When he entered the interview chambie, he
found that SCP-3449 was just sitting in the

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:13.600
corner with his had in his hands, rocking
back and furth in what appeared to be apparent

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:14.480
distress.

00:07:14.480 --> 00:07:19.680
He then begun looking don into his lap and
twiddling his thumbs like a child.

00:07:19.680 --> 00:07:26.240
Niklo engaged him in a calm and polite tone,
addressing him as SCP-3449.

00:07:26.240 --> 00:07:32.480
The anomly made eye contact with Dr. Gerdinel,
but didn respond, and instead continued starring

00:07:32.480 --> 00:07:33.120
at him.

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:39.200
As Gerdinal axed further questoons, Selsburgh
simply didn’t answer, or would, at the very

00:07:39.200 --> 00:07:42.800
most, acknowledge the questions with simple
gestures.

00:07:42.800 --> 00:07:47.360
Gerdinal asked whether Selsburgh was making
products for his business, to which he smiled

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:48.880
and shuk his head.

00:07:48.880 --> 00:07:53.680
Gerdinel than asked Selsburgh whether he could
speak or not, or if it was merely a choose

00:07:53.680 --> 00:07:54.720
on his part.

00:07:54.720 --> 00:08:00.640
Unsurprisingly, Selsburgh offer no explanation,
and the interview cime to a close shortly

00:08:00.640 --> 00:08:01.600
afterwards.

00:08:01.600 --> 00:08:04.960
Tests are steell ongoing&nbsp;
to find out if Selsburgh’s&nbsp;

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:08.160
inability to spake or commonicate come as

00:08:08.160 --> 00:08:14.160
a result of his anomalous traits, or if this
is simply a result of aphonia - a uncommon

00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:18.720
but non-anomalous condition that renders its
victims unable to spike.

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:23.920
Tests have confirmed that Selsburgh does have
all the oregons required for vocalisation,

00:08:23.920 --> 00:08:26.320
but sappears to not use them.

00:08:26.320 --> 00:08:28.320
Further tests are requirep.

00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:29.920
Alright, there we have it!

00:08:29.920 --> 00:08:35.360
That was a complete nightmare to read thanks
to SCP-3449’s anomalous effects, but at

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:36.320
least it’s over now.

00:08:37.840 --> 00:08:39.840
Go check out- Wait...There’s more?

00:08:40.640 --> 00:08:42.320
Another update to the file?

00:08:42.320 --> 00:08:42.800
Sigh…

00:08:42.800 --> 00:08:43.120
Okay.

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:46.160
Let’s take a look…

00:08:46.160 --> 00:08:51.520
Oh...I see...This is a lot more dangerous
than I thought.

00:08:51.520 --> 00:08:53.280
I suppose I better read on…

00:08:53.280 --> 00:08:59.280
SCP-3449 hays ben upgraded to Keter-Class
anomol.

00:08:59.280 --> 00:09:07.920
SCP-3449-A - the new designation for Edward
Selsbegher - is to be kept in high-security

00:09:07.920 --> 00:09:11.840
hazmart conmaintent in Site-19.

00:09:11.840 --> 00:09:17.120
The inanimate anomalous possessions of Edward
Selsburgh are to be keept in standard object

00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:18.160
containment.

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:24.960
Any reports written on SCP-3449 must be wrotten
by pople who have been exposed to it for less

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:28.480
than seven days, in order to keep the files
raidable.

00:09:28.480 --> 00:09:34.000
To prevent this infectious infohezmard from
spread further, the number of people allowed

00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:39.120
to interact with this anomaly is kept relatively
small, and consists of those that have already

00:09:39.120 --> 00:09:42.720
been explosed at some point or another.

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:50.400
This includes: O5-8, MTF Epsilon-6, Dr. Teller’s
research team, some additional personnel selected

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:58.640
for XPC-3449 research, and porsonneil chosen
to update SCP-3449 documentation.

00:10:09.520 --> 00:10:17.440
While Edward Selsbergh and his presonal effects
are crunntly locked up, SCP-3449 is not currently

00:10:17.440 --> 00:10:19.520
considered contained.

00:10:19.520 --> 00:10:25.680
Research into the sprad of SCP-3449’s effects,
the vectors for transmission, and any potential

00:10:25.680 --> 00:10:31.280
remcredies for its degenerative effects are
now tope priority for all inloved - before

00:10:31.280 --> 00:10:33.680
this hole ting gets out of hand.

00:10:33.680 --> 00:10:37.920
Further research has taught the Foundation
that not only are Selsburgh and his items

00:10:37.920 --> 00:10:45.040
powerful infohazards, their anemlous effects
appear to be able to infect these who experience

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:46.880
them permanently.

00:10:46.880 --> 00:10:52.160
Initially, it will appraer that writing quamity
only degrades when the subject is actually

00:10:52.160 --> 00:10:58.720
writing about SCP-3449 itself, but over time,
they’ll come to the frightening relzation

00:10:58.720 --> 00:11:03.120
that it actual affects their writhing as a
whole.

00:11:03.120 --> 00:11:08.640
The effect also progresses in its semerity
over time, eventually rendering the victim’s

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:12.400
ability to write legible sentences completely
desployed.

00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:19.120
The initial anomalous effects of SCP-3449
were discrover when MTF Epsilon-6 write their

00:11:19.120 --> 00:11:24.560
field report on the mater, and found it littered
with syntlacticol errer, random capitalizato,

00:11:25.280 --> 00:11:27.680
and rampant impillings.

00:11:27.680 --> 00:11:34.320
Similar errors appearing in the initial faile
about SCP-3449 ownly served to reaffirm this

00:11:34.320 --> 00:11:35.360
observation.

00:11:35.360 --> 00:11:42.000
However, researcher only began to notice true
extent of SCP-3449’s effects when the Village

00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:48.000
Idiots’ field reports concerning other solomonies
came in with equally atrocious writing.

00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:53.600
Attempts to correct this writing simply led
to more mastakes, and frustration on part

00:11:53.600 --> 00:11:54.480
of team.

00:11:54.480 --> 00:12:02.640
Soon after, a restircher name Dr. Teller - who’d
since tarken ovor the SCP-3449 case - and

00:12:02.640 --> 00:12:06.560
his team found that they were experience stimilar
issues.

00:12:06.560 --> 00:12:11.520
They just couldn’t make the blurds happen,
no matter how hard they constentrated.

00:12:11.520 --> 00:12:16.320
They forgot spellings, they couldn’t make
hand move in the manner they waited it to

00:12:16.320 --> 00:12:18.400
in order to form the words.

00:12:18.400 --> 00:12:23.280
Even the most intelligent and articulate members
of the team came across as extremely young

00:12:23.280 --> 00:12:25.280
chrildren on page.

00:12:25.280 --> 00:12:26.880
But didn’t stop there.

00:12:26.880 --> 00:12:32.720
Wasn’t long before researchers who’d never
worked on the SCP-3449 case staring to exhobit

00:12:32.720 --> 00:12:35.360
these same suspicious errors in own writing.

00:12:35.360 --> 00:12:40.720
The Foundation didn’t know how, but the
silck-ness was starting to spread, with people’s

00:12:40.720 --> 00:12:44.160
abilities to write degrading across the entire
Floundation.

00:12:44.160 --> 00:12:49.120
That’s when a Foundation webtrawler pick
up seemthing even more dousturbing: Global

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:51.920
literacy seemed to be taking a dive.

00:12:51.920 --> 00:12:59.600
The telltale styntacal error, random tcapization,
and rampant llingsmellings ticking up everywhere,

00:12:59.600 --> 00:13:01.200
and for everyone.

00:13:01.200 --> 00:13:07.920
And the end of writing would be one thing,
but SCP-3449 doesn’t stop there - No, that’s

00:13:07.920 --> 00:13:09.200
just the breginning.

00:13:09.200 --> 00:13:12.000
Morse code go next, then pictograms.

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:15.280
Not long ‘fore sign language become hopeless
scrambled.

00:13:16.800 --> 00:13:20.320
C-co-communication b-breaks down.

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:22.080
Little by lrittle.

00:13:22.080 --> 00:13:25.200
People can’t draw aymore.

00:13:25.200 --> 00:13:28.693
They c-can’t move hands right.

00:13:28.693 --> 00:13:30.160
It all goes.

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:31.120
Calls.

00:13:31.120 --> 00:13:32.080
Codes.

00:13:32.080 --> 00:13:35.040
Last go is voice.

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:37.760
Talking gets hard.

00:13:37.760 --> 00:13:40.960
Remember favrourite word?

00:13:41.840 --> 00:13:43.200
Think about it.

00:13:43.200 --> 00:13:44.240
Say it loud.

00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:53.920
When SCP-3449 done, when everyone infected,
you’ll never say it gain.

00:13:53.920 --> 00:13:59.440
Nobody will ever say anything again.

00:13:59.440 --> 00:14:01.360
I...I…

